{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>El</b> — Many commentators said: 'former ones' is an attribute for 'iniquities.' But the correct interpretation in my eyes: 'iniquities' is in construct state to 'former fathers,' and the word יקדמונו ('will precede us') corresponds to 'former ones.'" "And the meaning of 'for we are brought very low' — we have no strength and our hand has no El; therefore we seek compassion."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 79, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:28.356643069Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}